# BCT Delivery Flow

Use this as the default for BCT changes unless the user explicitly narrows or
overrides the scope.

1. Before changing anything, record the intended files, permitted deployment
   boundary, E2E success criteria, and protected UNKNOWN operations/claims.
2. Complete the focused regression, relevant local suite, static checks, and
   diff check before any LIVE change. Use the full suite when the affected
   boundary or repository gate requires it; do not make a reversible display
   correction wait on unrelated shards.
3. Use one of two explicit delivery lanes and record which lane applies:
   - **Reversible local-display lane**: Monitor-only HTML/CSS/rendering changes
     which do not alter Core/RCC/Native Host protocols, browser state, stored
     data, claims, messages, credentials, or external systems may be committed
     on the local authoritative main after local gates. Create a rollback
     backup, then run the exact-commit LIVE E2E while pushing the same commit
     and running CI in parallel. The work is complete only after both LIVE E2E
     and CI pass; either failure is recorded and the LIVE payload is rolled
     back when the display regression is material.
   - **Effectful lane**: Core, RCC, Native Host, wire/schema/security, database,
     claim, Chrome mutation, message send, or other externally visible effects
     require exact-head CI success before LIVE deployment or E2E effects.
4. Keep a coherent correction and its regression coverage in one exact commit
   or PR. For the effectful lane, prepare deployment and rollback while CI runs
   without changing LIVE. For the local-display lane, never let LIVE and CI
   test different commits.
5. Advance effectful E2E only in order: deployment health, one round trip,
   durable receipt/recovery, then the larger orchestration scenario.
6. Use compact status or presence for routine health. Request full DOM or RCC
   state only for a diagnosis, and label stale or uncertain observations rather
   than treating them as IDLE.
7. On a failed external effect, preserve the receipt and collect evidence
   (canonical text, DOM, ACK, active execution, pending receipt) before any
   retry. Never replay an UNKNOWN effect or release a protected claim merely
   to make progress.
8. Parallelize read-only inspection, test preparation, and GitHub observation.
   Keep shared worktree writes, browser sends, and LIVE mutations serialized.

Report the final state with the exact tested SHA, test/CI evidence, LIVE
evidence, E2E result, and any deferred follow-ups.
